<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Settings dialog (spec.md 15b file map, xrc-windows.md section E) - the
  frozen controls the canvas annotates plus the stock wxID_OK /
  wxID_CANCEL row, and F1's verbose_log_chk. Control names are frozen;
  tests find them with FindWindowByName and tools/gen_ids.py turns
  them into ui/ids.py (R-05, R-73).

  Measured on wxPython 4.3.1 / wxWidgets 3.3.3:

    * <value>1</value> and <style>wxRB_GROUP</style> are both honoured
      on wxRadioButton (tools/toolkit_probe.py check_xrc_names), so the
      appearance group opens and defaults here rather than in code.
    * <default>1</default> IS honoured on wxButton; the dialog's
      GetDefaultItem() returns wxID_OK.
    * XRC has no minsize property for windows - only for sizeritem and
      wxSplitterWindow (wxWidgets src/xrc/xmlres.cpp SetupWindow). No
      minimum is documented for this dialog, so it declares no <size>
      and the sizer handler Fit()s it and applies SetSizeHints().
    * wxSpinCtrlDouble honours <value>, <digits>, <inc>, <min> and a
      window <size> on the control itself (the dialog still declares
      none): avg_speed_spin loads at 12.0 and renders "12.0", and
      SetValue() floors anything below <min> at 1.0 - so the
      control's own half of the 1 km/h bound is structural, not
      code-side.

  Only the radio group and the average-speed entry declare a
  default. sound_chk, show_total_times_chk, show_lap_time_chk and
  verbose_log_chk are stored settings: the presenter loads them when
  the dialog opens, so no <checked> is declared for them. The two
  time-column checkboxes open on the presenter's own defaults (Total
  hidden, Lap time shown) rather than an authored <checked>.
  avg_speed_spin is both: its <value> is the 12.0 authoring default a
  bare load shows, and the presenter still seeds the stored value on
  open.

  Phase 1 (2026-09-13): avg_speed_spin replaced the old integer
  wxSpinCtrl with a one-decimal wxSpinCtrlDouble so the stored
  decimal speed survives the dialog (the spin's SetValue(round(...))
  used to truncate 12.5 to 12). Its caption is the frozen string
  "Avg Lap Time (kmh)", authored verbatim even though the value is
  the average rider speed in km/h. Plan §10: avg_speed_spin
  is the average rider speed the card-sufficiency estimate in
  Riders ▸ Check for Rider Issues… uses. Its <min> is 1 km/h so the
  entry cannot be parked at 0 (an infinite lap time); the stored
  value's own 1 km/h floor lives in the presenter (settings.py's
  _MIN_AVG_SPEED_KMH), this is the control's half of the same bound.

  Phase 1 also retired backup_now_btn (and its spacer row): the R-54
  manual backup keeps exactly one surface, File ▸ Back Up Database…
  (mi_backup_now). The dialog's only buttons are the stock pair.

  F1 (verbose logging): verbose_log_chk is a stored setting like
  sound_chk - AppSettings.verbose_logging, rendered at open and
  collected on OK. The app feeds it to ui.logging.Logging: it gates the
  trace methods of the single per-invocation structured log
  (rivercrossing-<timestamp>.log); the always-on launch/exception
  records and the log file itself ignore it.

  W13 (testing notes #12): the text-zoom choice (zoom_choice) left
  this dialog - View > Zoom is the single zoom surface, its seven
  90/100/110/120/130/140/150 rungs living on the mi_zoom_* menu items
  (main.xrc, spec.md 15b) for the 90-150% range of spec.md 13 / R-04.
  zoom_percent still persists through the settings file: the View
  menu's radios write it, startup applies it, and the dialog's OK
  carries it through untouched.

  The canvas notes the wxPython 4.2.5 baseline disabled the Dark radio
  with a "needs wxPython 4.3" hint. This build is 4.3.1 / wxWidgets
  3.3.3, so wxApp.SetAppearance exists and all three radios stay
  enabled; enabling state is code-side either way.

  Code-side per the canvas: loading and storing every value; applying
  the appearance choice through wxApp.SetAppearance;
  show_total_times_chk/show_lap_time_chk reaching the console
  mid-ride (each mirroring its own View-menu item).
-->
<resource>

  <object class="wxDialog" name="settings_dlg">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <!-- R-05 requires resizable windows (this dialog used to host the
         in-app text zoom, which cannot work in a fixed-size dialog;
         W13 moved zoom to the View menu and the dialog stays
         resizable per R-05). spec.md 13 says "dialogs fixed-size" -
         recorded conflict, resolved in favour of R-05. -->
    <style>wxDEFAULT_DIALOG_STYLE|wxRESIZE_BORDER</style>

    <object class="wxBoxSizer">
      <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStaticBoxSizer">
          <label>Appearance</label>
          <orient>wxVERTICAL</orient>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxBOTTOM</flag>
            <border>4</border>
            <object class="wxRadioButton" name="appearance_system_radio">
              <label>System</label>
              <style>wxRB_GROUP</style>
              <value>1</value>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxBOTTOM</flag>
            <border>4</border>
            <object class="wxRadioButton" name="appearance_light_radio">
              <label>Light</label>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="sizeritem">
            <object class="wxRadioButton" name="appearance_dark_radio">
              <label>Dark</label>
            </object>
          </object>

        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxCheckBox" name="sound_chk">
          <label>Sound on crossing (recorded / flagged / error cues)</label>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxCheckBox" name="show_total_times_chk">
          <label>Show Total Times on Crossings Panel</label>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxCheckBox" name="show_lap_time_chk">
          <label>Show Lap Time in Crossings Panel</label>
        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxCheckBox" name="verbose_log_chk">
          <label>Verbose logging (write a diagnostic log for support)</label>
        </object>
      </object>

      <!-- Plan §10 / Phase 1: the average rider speed the
           card-sufficiency estimate reads, as a one-decimal entry
           captioned with the frozen "Avg Lap Time (kmh)" string. A
           stored setting: the presenter seeds the stored value on
           open; the declared 12.0 is what a bare load shows. The
           60px width fits a 4-character value like "12.0". -->
      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxLEFT|wxRIGHT|wxTOP</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxBoxSizer">
          <orient>wxHORIZONTAL</orient>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL|wxRIGHT</flag>
            <border>6</border>
            <object class="wxStaticText">
              <label>Avg Lap Time (kmh)</label>
            </object>
          </object>

          <object class="sizeritem">
            <flag>wxALIGN_CENTRE_VERTICAL</flag>
            <object class="wxSpinCtrlDouble" name="avg_speed_spin">
              <value>12.0</value>
              <digits>1</digits>
              <inc>0.1</inc>
              <min>1</min>
              <size>60,-1</size>
            </object>
          </object>

        </object>
      </object>

      <object class="sizeritem">
        <flag>wxEXPAND|wxALL</flag>
        <border>10</border>
        <object class="wxStdDialogButtonSizer">
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_OK">
              <default>1</default>
            </object>
          </object>
          <object class="button">
            <object class="wxButton" name="wxID_CANCEL"/>
          </object>
        </object>
      </object>

    </object>
  </object>

</resource>
